<title>USA: Uruguay seeks oil prods to cover '97 refinery work.</title>
<headline>Uruguay seeks oil prods to cover '97 refinery work.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay's state oil refiner ANCAP, preparing for planned maintenance in early 1997 at its 34,600 barrel per day La Teja refinery, is tendering to buy refined products for February and March, traders said.</p>
<p>ANCAP is seeking 64,000 cubic metres (402,547 barrels) of gasoline, 105,000 cubic meters (660,429 barrels) of gas oil and 45,000 cubic metres (283,041 barrels) of fuel oil.</p>
<p>Officials at ANCAP were not immediately available to confirm the market talk. The refinery outage will begin around the end of January. ANCAP has said it plans to replace the refinery's catalytic cracker during the outage.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
